#N canvas 20 20 2600 2100 12;
#X text 20 20 c_mapped -- ONE DESTINATION'S SCALING AND ITS ROW ON THE SCREEN. u_map hands it the looked-up control as four floats \, it scales the value into the destination's own units \, passes the result on for the handler to act on \, and draws what the screen should say -- the mapped value while the control is live \, and both the latched value and where the control is pointing while parameter pickup holds it. Instantiated once per destination that carries a value \, which is why it is a c_ and not a u_: there is more than one \, and the scaling lives WITH its destination rather than once in the pickup machine and once in the handler., f 84;
#X text 20 220 creation arg 1: the ROW NAME as a makefilename format -- bpm \, or volca-cc%d where %d takes the map row's arg. REQUIRED. creation arg 2: the multiplier \, 127 for a MIDI value \, 490 for tempo. creation arg 3: the offset added after it \, 0 or 10. inlet 1: a list of four floats -- arg \, value 0 to 1 \, target 0 to 1 \, live 1 or 0. outlet 1: arg then the scaled value \, as a list \, ONLY WHILE LIVE., f 84;
#X text 20 400 ⛔ THE ACTION IS GATED HERE \, ON THE ASSEMBLED MESSAGE. While pickup holds a knob the handler must hear nothing -- not a stale value \, not a zero -- so the spigot sits on the pair rather than on either atom. The row still draws \, because a held control that says nothing cannot be told from a broken one (ref/module/map.md \, item 242). C-8 does not apply: nothing sits behind a reject here., f 84;
#X text 20 560 THE HELD ROW IS name <latched> (<knob>) -- bpm 57 (120). THE VALUE MUST BE A FLOAT because g_oled runs it through makefilename %g \, so the second number rides in the UNIT field as a free symbol. That is why there is a makefilename (%g) here rather than a second value. Item 240 is why the row lives here and not in u_map's pickup machine: built there it cannot know what the knob maps to \, and every armed knob announced itself as a bpm., f 84;
#X text 20 740 ORDER IS EVERYTHING BELOW AND unpack GIVES IT FOR FREE. Right to left: live sets the gate and is stored \, target is scaled and stored \, value is scaled and stored three times over \, and only then does arg arrive to name the row \, fire the action and choose which row to draw. Action first \, report second -- the same order every m_ layer uses. Two stores hold the scaled value because the live row and the held row each bang one \, and one store feeding both would draw both rows on every message (C-3)., f 84;
#X text 20 920 ⚠️ makefilename bpm WITH NO % IN IT STILL TAKES THE FLOAT AND IGNORES IT -- measured in 0.49 \, so a destination with no arg in its name needs no special case. ⚠️ The rounding is + 0.5 then i \, which is what stops a footer flickering between 119.7 and 120.1., f 84;
#X obj 20 1100 inlet;
#X obj 20 1160 unpack f f f f;
#X obj 1500 1240 t f f;
#X obj 1500 1330 f;
#X obj 1000 1240 * \$2;
#X obj 1000 1290 + \$3;
#X obj 1000 1340 + 0.5;
#X obj 1000 1390 i;
#X obj 1000 1450 f;
#X obj 500 1240 * \$2;
#X obj 500 1290 + \$3;
#X obj 500 1340 + 0.5;
